course: dictionary
lesson: 10257
title: Tonight and the time around us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you when something happens. Tonight is one of them. It means this evening or this night, the one that comes at the end of today. «Rain tonight, so take an umbrella» tells you the rain will come this evening, not now and not tomorrow.
explain: Look at the words around tonight to check its meaning. In «We're having beef tonight», the word tonight tells you when the dinner happens. If you swap in a time that does not fit, like «We're having beef yesterday», the sentence stops making sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
explain: Tonight can also be a noun, meaning the evening or night of today. Look at «Tonight's dinner smells great.» Here tonight's is about the dinner of this evening. Phrases like «later tonight» and «not tonight» use the same word in everyday talk.
fact: Tonight means this evening or this night, the night of today.
fact: As an adverb, tonight tells you when something happens, as in «Rain tonight».
fact: As a noun, tonight means the evening or night of today, as in «Tonight's dinner».
fact: Other time words work the same way: today, tomorrow and yesterday all tell you when.
fact: «We're having beef tonight» is a good example: in everyday talk, tonight is the time, and the dinner is the thing.
exercise: «Rain tonight, so take an umbrella.» What does tonight mean here? | Next week | Last summer | *This evening, the night of today | Every morning
exercise: «Grown-ups ask: am I in the mood for this feeling tonight?» Find and copy the word that tells you the time. | Grown-ups | *tonight | feeling | mood
exercise: Jayden says «Tonight's dinner smells great.» What does tonight's mean here? | A cold dinner | Tomorrow's breakfast | *Of this evening, the dinner of today's night | A dinner from last week
test: Priya's teacher said «Lovely, email it tonight then», but there was nothing to email. What time does tonight point to? | *This evening, today's night | Next Monday | Last night | Ages ago
test: In «We're having beef tonight», what kind of word is tonight? | A noun naming a thing | An adjective | *An adverb, telling us when | A verb
exam: In «a dance spin that failed tonight often works better tomorrow», which word tells you when the spin failed? | better | *tonight | tomorrow | often
